#[section, $md:
    @../ (Codebase) / Compiler-facing language reference

    # Compiler-facing language reference

    Compiler changes should start from the language contract. `docs/language-overview.md` remains the complete reference for syntax, semantics, edge cases and deferred language surface.
]

#[section, $md:
    ## Focused references

    Smaller detailed references are being prepared without changing the active authority during the migration.

    Foundations:

    - @../../language-overview (Language basics)
    - @../../bindings (Values and bindings)
    - @../../numbers (Numbers)
    - @../../casts (Casts)

    Functions and control flow:

    - @../../functions (Functions)
    - @../../branching (Branching)
    - @../../loops (Loops)
    - @../../errors (Errors, options and assertions)

    Data and compile-time construction:

    - @../../structs (Structs)
    - @../../choices (Choices)
    - @../../collections (Collections and maps)
    - @../../templates (Templates)
    - @../../constants (Constants and compile-time behaviour)

    Names and static abstraction:

    - @../../aliases (Aliases)
    - @../../generics (Generics)
    - @../../traits (Traits)

    UI state:

    - @../../reactivity (Reactivity)

    Projects and imported content:

    - @../../project-structure (Project structure)
    - @../../packages (Packages and imports)
    - @../../moth-templates (Moth template files)
    - @../../markdown (Plain Markdown)

    Each route combines a Basic teaching layer with detailed Advanced references. The unsuffixed Moth template files remain replacements under parity review and do not supersede `docs/language-overview.md` yet.
]

#[section, $md:
